### Question 6:

   Write a function that returns all possible combinations of k elements chosen from the n element set [a, b, c].
   For example, given n=3 and k=2, return [[a,b],[a,c], [b,c]].

#### Solution:
<details><summary>Click here</summary>  

```java
public class CombinationsOfKElementsFromNElementSet{
	static List<List<Integer>> getCombination(int [] arr, int size, int r){
		if(r==0)return Arrays.asList(new ArrayList<>());
		else if(size==0&&r!=0)return null;
		else{
			List<List<Integer>> res = new ArrayList<>();
			for(int i=0;i<=arr.length-r;++i){
				List<Integer> temp = new ArrayList<>();
				temp.addAll(Arrays.asList(arr).subList(i,i+r));
				res.addAll(getCombination(arr,size-1,r-1).stream().map((x)->{
					ArrayList<Integer> list = new ArrayList<>(x);
					list.add(arr[i]);
					return list;
				}).collect(Collectors.toList()));
			}
			return res;
		}
	}
	public static void main(String args[]){
		int arr[]={1,2,3};
		int k = 2;
		System.out.println(getCombination(arr,k));
	}
}
```

