The above code is an implementation of the [Knapsack Problem](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Knapsack_problem). The problem asks to find out which items are worth taking in order to maximize their total value while not exceeding the capacity of the knapsack. In this case, we have three different types of items with weights `3`,`4`,and `5`. We also know that our maximum weight allowed for the knapsack is `7`. This means that we can only take at most two items from each type. If we were able to fit all of them into the bag then it would be easy since we could just add up all the values of the items. However, because we cannot fit all of them into the bag, we need to choose wisely so as to maximize the value of the items we do end up fitting into the bag.

